### The comparison with the previous runs of a chapter, in the summary's
### dialog (src/engine/runs.ts), loaded when it first opens
### (src/texts/plugin.mjs: dialog-*.ftl). The "Replay this chapter" button
### and the summary's line are in interface.ftl.

compare-title = Compared with your previous runs
compare-intro = Your last runs of this chapter, kept in this browser only. Fewer commands is not a goal in itself: reading the manual, looking around and checking your work are part of the job.
compare-caption = Your runs of this chapter
compare-col-measure = Measure
# { $date }: the day of an earlier run, spelled out
compare-col-run = Run of { $date }
compare-col-this = This run
compare-exam = (exam mode)
compare-commands = Commands typed
compare-distinct = Different commands
compare-errors = Commands that failed
compare-hints = Hints asked for
compare-time = Time spent
compare-not-measured = not measured
# After this run's value, compared with the run just before it.
compare-better = down from last time
compare-worse = up from last time
compare-same = same as last time
compare-diff-title = Your commands, next to last time's
compare-diff-intro = In order: − only last time, + only this time, the others in both runs. The reference solution, step by step, is in the table above.
compare-only-before = Only last time:
compare-only-after = Only this time:
compare-both = Both times:
compare-diff-empty = No command typed in either run.
